9069.text:
9069 * phāṭṭakka 'gate, door'. [< * prahaṭṭa - ~ haṭṭa - ??] P. N. phāṭak m. 'gate'; A. phāṭak 'prison', phaṭak 'gate'; B. phā̆ṭak 'gate, prison'; Bi. H. phāṭak m. 'gate';
G. phaṭkiyũ bārṇũ n. 'a single shutter to close a door';
M. phāṭak , phākaṭ n., phaṭkā m. 'gate (of a village &c.)'. phāṇáyati ¹ 'makes spring' see pháṇati ¹. phāṇayati ² 'skims' see next.
